---
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout title="Pricing" description="LiteMCP Composer self-hosting is Apache-2.0 and call-home-free. Managed-cloud and design-partner commercial terms are invite-only and scoped after technical qualification; no public production plan is available yet.">
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Pricing"
    title="Free to self-host. Pilot terms follow technical fit."
    description="The public distribution is Apache-2.0 and has no hosted entitlement check, commercial quota, license server, mandatory telemetry, or call-home requirement. Managed-cloud and services pricing will be published only when the corresponding commitments are real."
    signal="Pre-1.0 · no public production plan"
  />

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="shell price-grid">
      <article class="price-card">
        <span class="price-card__label">Public distribution · Apache 2.0</span>
        <h2>Self-hosted source</h2>
        <div class="price-card__price">Free to use</div>
        <p>Evaluate, modify, and operate the public product without a private control plane or vendor account.</p>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>Governed local vertical slice with automated proof</li>
          <li>Portable Node, Docker Compose, and Helm assets</li>
          <li>Policy, approval, audit, and payload-free analytics</li>
          <li>No commercial self-hosting limit or call-home</li>
          <li>Production cluster and recovery acceptance still pending</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="button" href="/docs/getting-started#five-minute-proof">Run the five-minute proof</a>
      </article>
      <article class="price-card price-card--featured">
        <span class="price-card__label">Design partner · Invite only</span>
        <h2>Qualified governance pilot</h2>
        <div class="price-card__price">Scoped after fit</div>
        <p>Evaluate one high-risk MCP workflow against explicit technical and operating acceptance criteria.</p>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>Multiple MCP servers you already control</li>
          <li>One identity-scoped discovery and denial boundary</li>
          <li>One exact-context approval-gated action</li>
          <li>Customer-controlled or invite-only managed target</li>
          <li>No automatic account, acceptance, SLA, or price</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="button button--primary" href="/design-partners">Review fit and apply</a>
      </article>
      <article class="price-card">
        <span class="price-card__label">Managed cloud · Invite only</span>
        <h2>Operated preview</h2>
        <div class="price-card__price">No public price</div>
        <p>The current service track is for qualified pilots, not a generally available production subscription.</p>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>Same public product core as self-hosting</li>
          <li>Private operated-service customer controls</li>
          <li>Applications reviewed for technical fit</li>
          <li>No published uptime, capacity, or support commitment</li>
          <li>Current end-to-end service acceptance pending</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="button" href="/cloud">Inspect service status</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section content-section--subtle">
    <div class="shell split-layout">
      <div class="split-layout__aside">
        <p class="eyebrow">Plain-language model</p>
        <h2>A future hosted price will pay for operated responsibility, not permission to use the product.</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="principle-list">
        <li><span>01</span><div><strong>No placeholder price masquerades as validation</strong><p>Pilot and managed-cloud terms are scoped only after the workflow, deployment target, responsibilities, and acceptance criteria are understood.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>02</span><div><strong>Self-hosting remains independently operable</strong><p>The public distribution has no hosted entitlement check, mandatory call-home path, or commercial quota by default; operators may set their own governance limits.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>03</span><div><strong>Future service terms must name the responsibility</strong><p>Any paid plan must make capacity, environments, support, security response, upgrades, and reliability commitments explicit instead of implying them here.</p></div></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
